</tr>
<tr style="max-width:100%">
<td style="padding:0 20px 0 20px;text-align:left;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:16px;color:#000000;max-width:100%"></td>
</tr>
<tr style="max-width:100%">
<td style="padding-bottom:10px; min-width:100%; width:100%;max-width:100%"><!-- Inline styling used, as its an email content -->
<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentation" style="background-color:#121522; min-width:100%;max-width:100%">
<tbody>
<tr style="max-width:100%">
<td style="text-align:left;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12px;color:#FFFFFF;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;padding-top:10px;padding-bottom:10px;padding-left:20px;margin:0;max-width:100%" valign="middle">IN THE COURTS</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
<tr style="max-width:100%">
<td style="padding:0 20px 0 20px;text-align:left;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:16px;color:#000000;max-width:100%"><p style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:24px;line-height:24px;"><span style="color:#b70000;font-weight:bold;font-family:sans-serif;"><strong style="font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-weight:bold;">ON THE DOCKET:</strong> </span>The Supreme Court will hear oral arguments today for <i>Monsanto v. Durnell</i>, a case that has been at the center of the political battle over glyphosate, the active ingredient in the herbicide Roundup.</p>
<p style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:24px;line-height:24px;">The case weighs whether Bayer, which acquired Monsanto in 2018, should be preempted from failure-to-warn claims for cancer risks associated with pesticide use.</p>
<p style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:24px;line-height:24px;">It has been a political flash point between the Make America Healthy Again movement and the White House. The Trump administration <a href="https://url4027.email.politico.com/ss/c/u001.lWesBdxv006jasBZWiiGk9P_ybPe2CGyS-6CLrg5BxYWkXV4TejjmX9mNkoHKTH4K_8tBvNaxeCxodVnQ0nbMuQdrJRyB1u-IoYnyR4pa3rwttpMQ7qwZP3ML28FM2mZken6e4G2xEUroU7CwoavmlOT6llVpCCl5qFfQru1UKLBnluOhsqmhcM00P033wDe/4q5/NlalU5gmRhW8spN89i56Xw/h17/h001.veCsjKXQOejfl3pG4OGM6-r-QW87S45C6XZ8qF_uG5k" target="_blank">filed a brief</a> in December in support of the chemical company and released an executive order <a href="https://url4027.email.politico.com/ss/c/u001.6g0Zd3AyneOViJYBXgbV60SgT1lbNwilsYKFij_SeSSRfSECFHYbB9QTW5S-_OOYZZt3opHlBU2ysTooGOOapA159xUvyz16vOJoIgR6bpIp9TJcGxBLMapY6HAdtY73l-QLn6sZVYNMX1HNKsCL49s2h93c2dD6FZrBcqHgcI_LdXwa93spN9f4PfALHGimrUOuSG9f63GO_i36vaOLbuoHdcxYqSoUAP54yySwYSe0kRryTKYJmuKH80umhP3b/4q5/NlalU5gmRhW8spN89i56Xw/h18/h001.9uTmOYwe85WVl2gdnjPJxEja6PpE9IcikKmYU0N1IMY" target="_blank">aiming to boost production of glyphosate</a> earlier this year.</p>
<p style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:24px;line-height:24px;">MAHA leaders are hosting a rally titled “The People vs. Poison” at 9 a.m. in front of the high court. Speakers will include MAHA advocates Vani Hari and Tony Lyons and Reps. <a href="https://url4027.email.politico.com/ss/c/u001.2Z4DCAMF7Pq6fUenFyNGNTJibOcoTusa12Jh7uHsl_ykQ4p_ZxUtLl9VvXxUjv0xjZQPeYE2ioVySdnZxkO3CyFHQGQhsHDFCDSvlFU0DysMOrqwNbTpTF-jYu5xjZlB/4q5/NlalU5gmRhW8spN89i56Xw/h19/h001.Tb4GRDL4NCresRELCyhKt8cis7P6cZbXwFEcn6BhMfU" target="_blank">Chellie Pingree</a> (D-Maine) and <a href="https://url4027.email.politico.com/ss/c/u001.2Z4DCAMF7Pq6fUenFyNGNTJibOcoTusa12Jh7uHsl_ykQ4p_ZxUtLl9VvXxUjv0xcf8kxenCcMu4nBkENtapxoRZFPDm6EPBugyzZy5-YnfbUg9q3AfBo4hdJtc4icsG/4q5/NlalU5gmRhW8spN89i56Xw/h20/h001.oIwVUUmpIJDDJ7vnAr91x7NfXo_n6ATZJM6VTn6uHfU" target="_blank">Thomas Massie</a> (R-Ky.).<br/></p></td>
</tr>
