<p style="font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12px;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:10px;color:#000000;">A message from Bayer:</p>
<p style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:20px;line-height:24px;color:#000000;">Misinformation about agricultural science spreads faster than facts, creating uncertainty for farmers and policymakers alike. Yet here's what the data show: 88% of Republicans and 92% of Democrats agree rigorous science is necessary for progress. Americans haven't given up on evidence-based science - they're exhausted by viral misinformation and hungry for credibility.
     <br/>
<br/>
     A new survey conducted by The Harris Poll on behalf of Bayer on what Americans actually think about science and trust. The results reveal both challenge and opportunity - and shows policymakers that Americans value continued investment in research, innovation, and the scientific process.
     <br/>
<br/>
     See the findings for yourself and voice your support for science and the evidence-based outcomes it brings. <a href="https://url4027.email.politico.com/ss/c/u001.dgGKIUEMNqic94f5rSpPKCJCpfzLXKLU6KDtDs6qCfZLYYkmZS3PoJXUp0JefYNg4CAZLpDw6M0FiUvoie3nUg-rQf-oj49-fLA7vu_eAOJahl7to8Tmieaz0ljK53s_iDpSyJbBXoTvVoEjsEyoJXa6dzlgGDU6kO2Il8MpGjKUXtAdkj_ja-TRt82lKaEp/4q5/NlalU5gmRhW8spN89i56Xw/h26/h001.6w2MTiw62Qy917Vy4NcivhoFO5wkrpHnIMobS6H_NqQ" style="text-decoration:underline;color:#007BC7;" target="_blank">Learn more.</a></p>
