<td style="padding:0 20px 0 20px;text-align:left;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:16px;color:#000000;max-width:100%"><p style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:24px;line-height:24px;"><span style="color:#b70000;font-weight:bold;font-family:sans-serif;"><strong style="font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-weight:bold;">MA EXCLUSIVE:</strong> </span>The Center for the Environment and Welfare is rolling out an ad buy in the Washington, D.C., market this week in opposition to California’s Proposition 12, coinciding with the anticipated vote on the farm bill.</p>
<p style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:24px;line-height:24px;">The <a href="https://url4027.email.politico.com/ss/c/u001.6g0Zd3AyneOViJYBXgbV6wzH62Rc9P4qcO39WcxLMDeTTztLqbEiZhDzs9uFXqOCDXTrv5FLtYpYkocfvUCb8A/4q5/NlalU5gmRhW8spN89i56Xw/h27/h001.Uyls2lNvB2txrWojpa7Y1Mm5G3voTKGdI5h8DdTXzfA" target="_blank">commercial</a> argues Proposition 12 has elevated grocery prices. It will air on CNN, MSNBC’s “Morning Joe,” and Fox News’ “Fox &amp; Friends.”</p>
<p style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:24px;line-height:24px;">“Farmers have to spend millions and millions of dollars to rebuild barns to be California compliant,” the ad says. “Those costs are passed on to consumers across America, even if they don't live in California, and low-income Americans are being hit hardest.”</p>
<p style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:24px;line-height:24px;">“Congress is considering a fix that will help reduce your food costs and mix California's law before it gets worse,” it continues.</p>
<p style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:24px;line-height:24px;">Dozens of House Democrats recently <a href="https://url4027.email.politico.com/ss/c/u001.lWesBdxv006jasBZWiiGk9P_ybPe2CGyS-6CLrg5BxZPvQGMwjrcav6he_y4b0PEg8qNM8s4X8_QghSGYAmzoAYQGRG369Dl2L8bDT7Q495AVlpKzbi6ER3Lu5Vco_vc/4q5/NlalU5gmRhW8spN89i56Xw/h28/h001.FKPYKsJHsVfH7Y2AokdVjo9xVXUEsNJBUDN_Z9qzhUY" target="_blank">sent a letter</a> to the chamber’s leadership opposing the provision, and it’s unclear whether it will remain in the final text amid opposition from some Republicans including Garbarino.<br/></p></td>
