<p style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:24px;line-height:24px;"><strong style="font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-weight:bold;">— First lady Melania Trump announced </strong><a href="https://url4027.email.politico.com/ss/c/u001.zmXQYxftKFWCpJXVm9O1djndczjebkyFag2a72nzVMtBPv7MvtumVZAaB9JAhUXMmnxqISOi5e6Rqc0OPO_HM9W1faVlk8sk925KG0fhBIk/4q5/NlalU5gmRhW8spN89i56Xw/h30/h001.M1OiROVR9mzLLICtPHsXaViRBPV3RwO6nj2ODZNhNU8" target="_blank"><strong style="font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-weight:bold;">in a post on X</strong></a><strong style="font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-weight:bold;"> the addition of a beehive</strong> housing two colonies to the White House honey program.</p>
